url":"https://newport.moderngov.co.uk/ieListDocuments.aspx?CId=165&MId=9143"},{"date":"2027-01-26","committee":"Council","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://newport.moderngov.co.uk/ieListDocuments.aspx?CId=130&MId=9217"},{"date":"2027-01-28","committee":"Governance and Audit Committee","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://newport.moderngov.co.uk/ieListDocuments.aspx?CId=145&MId=9157"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-10-07","committee":"Formal Council Questions and Responses","time":"","status":"Confirmed; 2026/49: City Centre Footfall","webcast":false,"url":"https://newport.moderngov.co.uk/ieListDocuments.aspx?CId=525&MId=9303"},{"date":"2026-10-13","committee":"Performance Scrutiny Committee - People","time":"11.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.newport.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-14","committee":"Cabinet","time":"4.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.newport.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-15","committee":"Formal Council Questions and Responses","time":"","status":"Confirmed; 2026/52: Newport Transport","webcast":false,"url":"https://newport.moderngov.co.uk/ieListDocuments.aspx?CId=525&MId=9309"},{"date":"2026-10-22","committee":"Governance and Audit Committee","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Provisional","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.newport.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-22","committee":"Formal Council Questions and Responses","time":"","status":"Confirmed; 2026/44: Leadership Cohesion","webcast":false,"url":"https://newport.moderngov.co.uk/ieListDocuments.aspx?CId=525&MId=9316"},{"date":"2026-10-26","committee":"Delegated Decisions - Cabinet Member for Climate Change, Waste and Recycling","time":"","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://newport.moderngov.co.uk/ieListDocuments.aspx?CId=618&MId=9308"},{"date":"2026-10-26","committee":"Delegated Decisions - Deputy Leader / Cabinet Member for Education and Early Years","time":"","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://newport.moderngov.co.uk/ieListDocuments.aspx?CId=614&MId=9307"},{"date":"2026-10-28","committee":"Performance Scrutiny Committee - Partnerships","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Provisional","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.newport.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-05","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Management Committee","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.newport.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Newport forecasts \u00a30.746m overspend for 2026/27 after contingency, with services \u00a34.745m over","lead":"Newport City Council's September revenue monitoring report, going to Cabinet on 11 November, forecasts a net overspend of \u00a30.746m for 2026/27, against a net revenue budget of \u00a3462.8m. That figure takes the contingency budget into account. Service areas, excluding schools, are forecast to overspend by \u00a34.745m. The paper describes this as substantially offset by temporary underspends in non-service areas, including \u00a31.636m on general contingency and \u00a32.073m on capital financing.\n\nTwo services account for much of the service overspend. Housing Services is forecast to overspend by \u00a32.992m. Temporary accommodation payments to landlords and hotels are forecast \u00a31.1m over budget and income about \u00a31.0m below budget, and alarm and security provision is \u00a3953k over. Planned mitigation of \u00a3342k is not being delivered, and the paper says this will carry into 2027/28. Children's residential placements are forecast to overspend by \u00a32.170m. The paper attributes this to delays in new in-house capacity: 29 in-house placements across 11 properties are operating against 38 planned across 12. Nineteen children remain in out-of-area placements against a budget assumption of 11. Health and education contributions of \u00a3720k are expected to offset part of the cost.\n\nSchools are forecast separately to overspend their revenue funding by \u00a30.606m, met from school reserves. Balances are forecast to fall from \u00a313.054m brought forward to \u00a312.488m by March 2027. Forty-nine of 55 schools forecast an in-year overspend, two primary schools forecast a deficit, and about 59% of the forecast overspend funds recurring spending. The paper notes a Welsh Government additional learning needs grant of approximately \u00a32.5m may ease pressures.","iso":"2026-11-11","paper_title":"04 Final September 26 Revenue Cabinet Report","paper_url":"https://newport.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s37364/37364.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-11-11","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"05 Capital Monitoring and Additions - September 26","paper_url":"https://newport.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s37358/37358.pdf","headline":"The New Leisure Centre's building shell is approaching full completion, with internal fit-out ongoing.","detail":"The facility will be one of the first all-electric leisure facilities in Wales and will be operated by Newport Live upon completion. The Council is liaising with the trust on the programme for entry into service.","category":"capital","matters":"A major city-centre scheme reaching shell completion and moving to operator handover is a delivery milestone for a council in a similar position.","figures":"\u00a314.192m 2026/27 budget and forecast","quote":"The building shell is approaching full completion with progress ongoing in relation to the internal fit out.","read_on":"2026-11-06","material":true},{"iso":"2026-11-11","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"05 Capital Monitoring and Additions - September 26","paper_url":"https://newport.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s37358/37358.pdf","headline":"The Capital Financing Requirement is indicated to rise from \u00a3319.6m at 31.03.26 to \u00a3347.4m at 31.03.28, while debt is indicated to fall to \u00a3201.7m.","detail":"Debt is shown including PFI and leases and short- and long-term borrowing. The Council expects to remain within the requirement that actual debt stays below the capital financing requirement.","category":"borrowing","matters":"Debt falling while the capital financing requirement rises means more of the Council's need is met internally, which bears on future refinancing and new borrowing decisions.","figures":"CFR \u00a3319.6m (31.03.26 outturn), \u00a3327.2m (31.03.27 indicative), \u00a3347.4m (31.03.28 indicative), \u00a3344.2m (31.03.29 indicative); debt \u00a3253.1m (31/03/26 outturn), \u00a3201.7m (31/03/28 indicative)","quote":"TOTAL CFR 322.7 319.6 327.2 347.4 344.2","read_on":"2026-11-06","material":true},{"iso":"2026-11-11","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"05 Capital Monitoring and Additions - September 26","paper_url":"https://newport.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s37358/37358.pdf","headline":"The Chief Financial Officer says elevated interest rates have increased the financing costs of the capital programme, with future investment needed from 2028/29 if rates do not fall.","detail":"The forecast 2026/27 capital financing costs are \u00a325.1m against a budget of \u00a327.1m, which is 5.42% of net revenue stream against a 5.80% budget. The capacity to borrow from the revenue budget is being reviewed.","category":"borrowing","matters":"Financing costs shown against budget, and a stated revenue investment requirement tied to interest rates, bear on the affordability of the same borrowing for councils in similar positions.","figures":"\u00a325.1m forecast financing costs; \u00a327.1m 2026/27 budget; 5.42% forecast proportion of net revenue stream; 5.80% budgeted proportion; \u00a326.8m 2027/28 budget; \u00a326.7m 2028/29 budget","quote":"This has increased the financing costs of the capital programme and will require future investment from 2028/29 if interest rates do not fall in the short to medium term.","read_on":"2026-11-06","material":true},{"iso":"2026-11-11","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"05 Capital Monitoring and Additions - September 26","paper_url":"https://newport.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s37358/37358.pdf","headline":"The Chief Financial Officer states the Council's borrowing requirement is accelerating due to new projects and reducing reserves.","detail":"The Chief Financial Officer says the challenge this brings to budget setting is significant, and that scope for projects funded from new borrowing above the \u00a318m general headroom is extremely limited.","category":"borrowing","matters":"A finance officer at a peer council, or a lender, would want to see the Chief Financial Officer link a rising borrowing requirement to falling reserves in the same paper.","figures":"\u00a318m general borrowing headroom added","quote":"The Council\u2019s borrowing requirement is accelerating due to new projects as well as reducing reserves and the challenge this brings to the budget setting is significant.","read_on":"2026-11-06","material":true},{"iso":"2026-11-11","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"05 Capital Monitoring and Additions - September 26","paper_url":"https://newport.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s37358/37358.pdf","headline":"The Council reports no new capital schemes funded by borrowing so far in 2026/27.","detail":"The Council's prudential indicators record the borrowing limits for new capital expenditure alongside this position.","category":"borrowing","matters":"A council with no new borrowing-funded schemes this year, but a rising capital financing requirement, shows how borrowing decisions are being staged.","figures":"","quote":"There have been no new capital schemes funded by borrowing so far within 2026/27","read_on":"2026-11-06","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-11-03"},"name":"Newport","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-11-06","since_iso":"2026-10-07","distress":false,"headline":"17 new committee papers landed","lead":"The newest was \u201cTaxi Licensing Code of Practice\u201d from Licensing (Taxi) Panel on 2026-11-03.","also":["17 papers caught"],"watch":"Cabinet on 2026-11-11","n_findings":0,"n_documents":17,"top_paper_title":"Taxi Licensing Code of Practice","top_paper_url":"https://newport.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s37117/37117.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":177,"news_drafts_total":1}}